{{also|Appendix:Variations of "ac"}}
==Turkish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tr|ota|آج|tr=āc||hungry}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-oat|tr=ac|||hungry}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*āç}}, {{m|trk-pro|*ạ̄č||hunger}}.
{{rel-top|cognates}}
Cognate with {{cog|xqa||tr=āç||hunger, hungry}}, {{cog|otk|𐰀𐰲|tr=aç||hunger, hungry}}, {{cog|az|ac||hungry}}, {{cog|ba|ас||hungry}}, {{cog|cv|выҫӑ||hungry}}, {{etyl|kk|-}} & {{cog|tyv|аш||hungry}}, {{cog|ky|ач||hungry}}, {{cog|tk|aç||hungry}}, {{cog|uz|och||hungry}}, {{cog|sah|аас||hunger}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ɑtʃ]|lang=tr}}

===Noun===
{{tr-noun|ı|lar}}

# {{label|tr|archaic}} [[hunger]]
#: {{ux|tr|'''''Acımdan''' ölüyorum.''|I am dying '''of hunger'''.|inline=1}} {{gloss|Literally '''of my hunger'''}}
# [[hungry]], [[esurient]] or [[greedy]] person or people
#: {{ux|tr|'''''Aç''' ne yemez tok ne demez.''|'''Hungry person''' eats anything, satieted person complains of everything.|inline=1}} {{gloss|A proverb}}

====Usage notes====
*The noun has two declension forms. One normal and one with /ç/→/c/.

